{
  "_comment": [
    "Evaluation set for travel_assistant.graph._merge_extracted.",
    "",
    "Each case is one user utterance and the fields a correct extraction",
    "would produce. `null` is a real expectation, not 'don't care': the",
    "most damaging small-model failure here is inventing a plausible value",
    "for a field the user never mentioned (group_type='solo' when nobody",
    "said who is travelling), which then flows into the plan unchallenged.",
    "The harness scores those as hallucinations separately from misses.",
    "",
    "`tags` group cases by the mechanism they exercise so a regression can",
    "be attributed to a specific piece of defensive logic."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "full-front-loaded",
      "utterance": "I'm planning a 7-day family trip to Japan with a moderate budget, we love food and temples.",
      "tags": ["happy-path"],
      "expected": {"destination": "Japan", "trip_length_days": 7, "group_type": "family", "interests": "food, temples", "budget_level": "moderate"}
    },
    {
      "id": "destination-only",
      "utterance": "I want to go to Lisbon.",
      "tags": ["grounding", "sparse"],
      "expected": {"destination": "Lisbon", "trip_length_days": null, "group_type": null, "interests": null, "budget_level": null}
    },
    {
      "id": "no-group-stated",
      "utterance": "Five days in Rome, I'm into art museums, keeping it cheap.",
      "tags": ["grounding"],
      "expected": {"destination": "Rome", "trip_length_days": 5, "group_type": null, "interests": "art museums", "budget_level": "budget"}
    },
    {
      "id": "wife-and-son-implies-family",
      "utterance": "Taking my wife and son to Orlando for 4 days.",
